Goemon's Great Adventure (Nintendo 64) - decompilation credits

This decompilation stands on the work of the N64 decompilation community. Every tool,
library and project below was used or consulted to build it, and each credit was checked
against the project's own source (its git history, README, LICENSE or package metadata).
Authors are named as each project names them; "and contributors" means many more people
whose work is in it.


SPECIAL THANKS
==============

Tools that build this decompilation
-----------------------------------

splat - splits the ROM into assembly, data and C stubs, and writes the linker script
  Ethan Roseman (ethteck), with Anghelo Carvajal, Alex Bates, Mark Street and contributors
  https://github.com/ethteck/splat

spimdisasm and rabbitizer - splat's MIPS disassembler and instruction decoder
  Anghelo Carvajal (AngheloAlf), Decompollaborate
  https://github.com/Decompollaborate/spimdisasm
  https://github.com/Decompollaborate/rabbitizer

asm-processor - lets IDO compile C files that still hold functions as assembly
(#pragma GLOBAL_ASM); every game C file and the zlib objects go through it
  Simon Lindholm, with Anghelo Carvajal, Dragorn421, EllipticEllipsis, Mr-Wiseguy and
  contributors
  https://github.com/simonlindholm/asm-processor

ido-static-recomp - the IRIX IDO 5.3 and 7.1 compilers, statically recompiled to run on
modern machines
  Emil Lenngren (original author); decompals: Ethan Roseman, Anghelo Carvajal, cadmic,
  Derek Hensley and contributors
  https://github.com/decompals/ido-static-recomp

IDO (IRIS Development Option) 5.3 and 7.1 - the original C compilers the game was built
with (7.1 for the game and zlib, 5.3 for libultra)
  Silicon Graphics, Inc.

GNU Binutils (mips64-elf as, ld, objcopy, objdump, ar)
