  devkitPro: https://devkitpro.org
  MSYS2 (runtime forked from Cygwin): https://www.msys2.org
  GCC and GNU make: the GNU Project / Free Software Foundation

Python - every build and analysis tool here is Python
  The Python Software Foundation; created by Guido van Rossum
  https://www.python.org


Libraries in the game
---------------------

ultralib - the decompiled libultra (the N64 SDK library); its sources build and match the
game's libultra 2.0I/2.0J objects, and its headers serve the game's C
  decompals: Derek Hensley, Mr-Wiseguy, Anghelo Carvajal, Tharo, Ethan Roseman and
  contributors
  https://github.com/decompals/ultralib

zlib 1.1.3 - the game's file decompressor, built from the original source
  Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler
  https://github.com/madler/zlib


Tools used to write it
----------------------

decomp-permuter - searches for C that compiles to the game's instructions
  Simon Lindholm, with Synray, Dane Bouchie and contributors
  https://github.com/simonlindholm/decomp-permuter

m2c (formerly mips_to_c) - the first C draft of each file
  Matt Kempster and Zach Banks (authors); maintained by Simon Lindholm, with contributors
  https://github.com/matt-kempster/m2c

asm-differ - compares the built functions with the game's
  Simon Lindholm, with Léo Lam, Chippy, Ethan Roseman, Mark Street and contributors
  https://github.com/simonlindholm/asm-differ

pycparser - the C parser inside decomp-permuter and m2c
  Eli Bendersky
  https://github.com/eliben/pycparser

n64sym - identifies libultra functions by their bytes
  shygoo
  https://github.com/shygoo/n64sym

IDA Pro - used to study the game's own code (the Konami LZ decompressor)
  Hex-Rays SA
  https://hex-rays.com/ida-pro


